          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly avows the narrator's love for Maria as true. It answers her request for assurance that his present feeling is real and will not be regretted tomorrow.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"jeg tvivler ikke længer\\nom min egen\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the avowal is framed as a solemn assurance and immediately expanded into love enduring through pleasure, hardship, ordinary days, and celebrations. The same turn places that love within a proposed lifelong shared bond. Those statements are distinct propositions, but they establish the focal avowal's force as affirming an enduring relational undertaking rather than merely reporting a present feeling. It is not yet a formal marriage vow and its practical terms remain broad.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is intensely emotional, the focal words are a deliberate answer to Maria's question and form a truth-claim and assurance. The evidence does not present them as a reflex-like or uncontrolled affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din\\nElskerinde?\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.89,\"reason\":\"The focal expression's central work is adequately captured by avowal and contextually supported relational undertaking. Its reassuring function is the interpersonal purpose of those modes rather than a separate residual force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At their reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's changed attitude is genuine, not temporary longing and not something he will regret the next day. He answers her directly with the focal declaration, then describes love enduring across changing circumstances and a desire to live a long life with her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The narrator affirms an enduring bond: loving Maria in pleasure and hardship, on ordinary and festive days, and sharing a long life before dying together. Maria's tears and the narration that she understands him to be speaking truly and is happy represent positive uptake. The passage does not specify formal terms within the focal words themselves; the undertaking force comes from their oath-like framing and expansion in the same turn.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work with sufficient confidence from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The literary narration strongly represents sincere affection and successful uptake, but it cannot independently verify inner sincerity outside that representation. The focal phrase alone is a simple avowal; its substantial undertaking force depends on Maria's preceding question and the remainder of the narrator's same reply.\"}"
